{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186985-noah-s-ark-changing-bleeds-lost-tribes","id":1186985,"title":"Noah's Ark! (Changing Bleeds & lost Tribes)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-17T01:41:41-08:00","id":1186985,"title":"Noah's Ark! (Changing Bleeds & lost Tribes)","content":"I have been wanted to do a Changing breed/ lost tribes log and game for some time. I have been very interested in the War of Rage and reasons for different animal kinds have been lost!<br /> <br /> It took me only a short while to hit the Noah's ark idea.<br /> <br /> How anyone can help!<br /> <br /> If you know of a shifter or Lost breed of any tribe. Name it and what animal it may be and where they are:<br /> <br /> LIke:<br /> <br /> Garou; Wolves; Werewolf the Apocalypse (entire book); global<br /> <br /> Maybe if you feel what are some ways to bring them back or where could they be hiding?<br /> <br /> I am keeping it to classic world of darkness and W20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T06:59:32-08:00","id":1187032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alstonjc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186985-noah-s-ark-changing-bleeds-lost-tribes#post1186985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe if you feel what are some ways to bring them back or where could they be hiding?<br /> <br /> I am keeping it to classic world of darkness and W20</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an almost forgotten Mokol\u00e9 rite, the <b>Rite of the Sleeping Dragon</b> (Mokol\u00e9 Breed Book p.93) wich enables you to put another one in Dragon Sleep, like the same named Gift<br /> Essentialy, the ritemaster need to cover the sleeper (mud, or coffing, etc) and use the rite... and thats all ^^<br /> The Gift - wich the Rite mimics - enebales the sleeper to sleep thrugh ages, no maximum years, how long one could slumber. - like the Torpor of vampires just without drawback (except the trauma the world changed, whats happened, or if you are an evil Storyteller, the posions and polution in the air is too much them to handle, need to find a way to help them adapt to the new enviroment - or watch them suffer and eventually die)<br /> So I think it quite possible, some clever Mokole &quot;burried&quot; entire villages of kinfolk / shifters with this in caves, underground temples when the Garou went insane murderhobos... and now, the War is over and Gaia needs her children more than ever, via Mnesis the good lizards remember where to find them and roar the wake up call<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T16:55:38-08:00","id":1187166,"title":"","content":"ohh the is cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>&quot;Don't worry, it'll work out somehow.&quot; - <br /> <i>You Asakura (Shaman King)</i></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23653-alstonjc","name":"Alstonjc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T17:43:51-08:00","id":1187181,"title":"","content":"I suspect that there used to be bird shifters among raptors similar to the ones in Forsaken's War Against the Pure, but that's just me. <br /> <br /> As far as I know, the only ones officially listed outside of the tribe and breed books were aurochs, hogs, and bats, and the lost White Howler, Croatan and Bunyip tribes, but it's not that hard to develop new ones. If the Changelings hadn't already taken them, I'd suggest Selki were seals. Werehares, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3